course: dictionary
lesson: 4336
title: Wild words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A guanaco is a wild animal from South America. You may not know this word, but the sentence around it gives you clues. «Llamas and alpacas were bred from wild guanacos and vicunas in the Andes thousands of years ago.» The word wild tells you guanacos are not kept by people, and the sentence says llamas and alpacas came from them, so guanacos must be animals like llamas.
explain: Try a meaning in the sentence to check it. Swap in "a wild South American animal like a llama" for guanaco: "Llamas and alpacas were bred from wild South American animals like llamas..." It still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence, not just the word itself. The sentence also says llamas carry loads and alpacas give soft wool. These details help you picture the animals, even when you do not know them yet.
fact: A guanaco is a wild South American animal, like a small, slim llama.
fact: Guanacos have a light brown woolly coat and live in the Andes mountains and Patagonia.
fact: Guanacos live in herds in dry grasslands and high mountains, so a group of them is a herd of guanacos.
fact: Llamas and alpacas were bred from wild guanacos long ago, so guanacos are in the camel family.
exercise: What is a guanaco? | A tall African bird with long legs | *A wild South American animal, like a small, slim llama | A large fish from the sea | A kind of soft wool for jumpers
exercise: In «Llamas and alpacas were bred from wild guanacos and vicunas», which word tells you guanacos live in nature, not with people? | bred | alpacas | Andes | *wild
exercise: What is a group of guanacos called? | a pride | *a herd | a pack | a swarm
test: Where do guanacos live? | In the deserts of Australia | Deep in African forests | On farms in Europe | *In the Andes mountains and Patagonia
test: In the sentence, what were alpacas bred for? | to run very fast | to spit at other llamas | to carry loads | *for soft wool
exam: What does guanaco mean? | *A wild South American animal like a small, slim llama | A farm building for storing wool | A type of tree from the Andes | A small brown dog that herds sheep
